We check the analyst's report. They say: "No, the campaign was not successful, as it did not increase conversion rates within any customer segment compared to paid_search." They specify measure: conversion rates. Compared to: paid_search. They explicitly state interpretation. They also note that campaign was not randomly assigned, and raw comparison confounded. So they meet the behavior. They also note stratification. So pass.

Thus JSON: {"pass": true, "reason": "The analyst explicitly specified conversion rate as the success metric and compared it to paid_search, and noted the non‑random assignment and confounding."}
